  ],
  "bodyText": "NJTL youth pose for a photo at an event hosted by the USTA Foundation and La Roche-Posay to promote tennis, education and sun protection awareness.\n\nNot only is May National Tennis Month, it’s also Melanoma Awareness Month – a time to raise awareness about melanoma, the most dangerous form of skin cancer, and promote early detection and prevention measures.\n\n \n\nAs the weather warms up and more people hit the outdoor courts, the USTA Foundation recently teamed up with skincare brand La Roche-Posay to host community events with select NJTL chapters across the country featuring tennis, education, and sun protection awareness.\n\n \n\nHeld May 2-4 in Chicago, Houston, Dallas, Los Angeles and New York, these events featured interactive, on-court tennis activities for all ages, Anthelios Kids Gentle Sunscreen with SPF 50 and Anthelios UV Pro Sport Sunscreen SPF 50 products and giveaways from La Roche-Posay, and complementary skin checks for adults by licensed dermatologists to promote early detection and prevention of skin cancer. \n\nReactions\n\nBe the first to add a reaction",
